<article class="env-example" id="043L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/043L">Example <span data-tag="043L">78.7.3</span> <span class="named">(Additive group algebraic space)</span>.</a>  Let $B \to S$ as in Section <a href="/tag/043A" data-tag="043A">78.3</a>. Consider the functor which associates to any scheme $T$ over $B$ the group $\Gamma (T, \mathcal{O}_ T)$ of global sections of the structure sheaf. This is representable by the group algebraic space </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathbf{G}_{a, B} = B \times _ S \mathbf{G}_{a, S}  \]
</div>
  <p> over $B$. Here $\mathbf{G}_{a, S}$ is the additive group scheme over $S$, see Groupoids, Example <a href="/tag/022V" data-tag="022V">39.5.3</a>. </p>
</article>